# spore-conformance.mdc

meta:
  name: Spore Conformance
  description: >
    Defines the requirements and validation criteria for spore distribution and validation.
    Ensures spores meet project standards for distribution and review.

rules:
  - when: spore.distribution
    then:
      - "Spores must be saved to $HOME/Downloads for distribution"
      - "Spores must be in a format that preserves all necessary metadata and validation information"
      - "Spores must include validation information that can be verified by the project's validation tools"

  - when: spore.validation
    then:
      - "Spores must be semantically valid according to the project's ontology model"
      - "Spores must include appropriate documentation that explains their purpose and usage"
      - "Spores must clearly specify any dependencies or requirements for their use"

  - when: spore.review
    then:
      - "Spores must be reviewed according to the project's review procedures"
      - "Documentation must be reviewed for completeness and accuracy"
      - "Validation results must be reviewed and verified"

  - when: spore.integration
    then:
      - "Spores must be properly modeled in the project's ontology"
      - "Spores must integrate with the project's validation and review tools"
      - "Spores must be properly documented in the project's documentation system"

  - when: spore.maintenance
    then:
      - "Spores must be version controlled"
      - "Changes to spores must be tracked and documented"
      - "Deprecated spores must be clearly marked and documented"

rationale: >
  These requirements ensure that:
  - Spores are properly distributed and accessible
  - Spores can be validated and verified
  - Spores are properly documented and maintained
  - Spores integrate with the project's tools and processes
  - Spores meet the project's quality standards

---
This rule helps ensure spores meet project standards for distribution and review.
